       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg per day for extended-release. Single doses are usually 1,000 mg or less.\n- **Risk:** This is about twice the maximum daily dose. It could cause lactic acidosis and severe GI effects.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg three times daily, which is 2,550 mg per day and the max\n- 850 mg twice daily, which is 1,700 mg per day\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into other doses\n- Another dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, please confirm that. I'd also suggest adding a note with the clinical rationale."
